<title>GERMANY: Dresdner shares slip on Moody's rating news.</title>
<headline>Dresdner shares slip on Moody's rating news.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Dresdner Bank AG slipped in Friday trading on news that U.S. ratings agency Moody's Investors Service said the outlook for the bank's long-term and financial strength ratings was negative.</p>
<p>Dresdner Bank shares, which had posted gains until minutes before the news was released, fell 35 pfennigs to 40.30 shortly afterwards.</p>
<p>The broader DAX index was also down 0.31 percent at 2,658.18 points.</p>
<p>The ratings agency said it had termed the long-term financial strength as &quot;negative&quot;, altering the outlook from &quot;stable&quot;.</p>
<p>The bank's senior unsecured debt however remains unchanged at &quot;Aaa&quot;.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
